# Database and security

Follow technical guide §20 and the `supabase` + `supabase-postgres-best-practices` skills.

## Rules

- PostgreSQL is the system of record for bookings, sessions, roles, transcripts, reports, consent, events, and jobs
- Enable RLS on every exposed table, including tables with no user policy yet
- Browser clients only access what RLS permits; privileged writes go through server services
- Schema changes via SQL migrations only; regenerate types after migrations
- Never change a migration that has reached production — add a new one
- Preview/local must never point at production DB, LiveKit, email, or payment
- Do not log secrets, auth headers, magic links, provider tokens, or raw cookies
- Prefer EU-region Supabase for the MVP

## Data minimization

- 18+ confirmation only — no DOB, passport, nationality, or official exam credentials
- Do not put transcript text, emails, names, tokens, or hidden role content in analytics
- Deletion is a documented cross-system workflow, not “delete from UI” alone

When reviewing auth/RLS changes, also apply the `security-best-practices` skill.
